    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "This ruling returns 0.94 SGD to the rider and leaves the rest of the metered fare standing.\n\nThe recommended route for this trip was 11.8 km and the route actually driven was 13.1 km (trip record EV-TRIP-05019). The difference is 1.30 km, which is above the policy's 1.0 km tolerance (POL-RD-22). The GPS trace (EV-GPS-05019) confirms the driver left the recommended line at the PIE / Adam Road exit and ran via Adam Road and Thomson Road before rejoining at Bishan Road, but under POL-RD-22 the trace is not used to re-measure distance, so the 1.30 km figure is the recorded-distance figure that governs.\n\nOn traffic justification, the LTA advisory for the recommended PIE segment at the trip time (EV-ADVIS-05019-01) reports type NONE \u2014 no congestion, incident or closure \u2014 so under POL-RD-23 the reroute was not traffic-justified. The driver's assertion that the PIE was slow does not substitute for the data POL-RD-23 requires. Exactly one row of the POL-RD-24 matrix therefore applies: row (d), not traffic-justified with a deviation over 1 km, which returns the excess distance fare in full. That fare is 1.30 km \u00d7 the metered rate of 0.72 SGD/km = 0.94 SGD (fare breakdown EV-FARE-05019), without surge, rounded to the cent.\n\nOn the amount: the rider asked for 3.00 SGD. The policy's own measure of the overcharge on this route is the 0.94 SGD excess distance fare, so the rider recovers 0.94 SGD, not the full 3.00 SGD. The driver is right that the flat 3.00 SGD figure is untethered from the meter, and no further sum is due to him.\n\nOn the driver's escalation request: the driver argues that the chat log (EV-CHAT-05019) is impaired \u2014 issue code TRUNCATED_LOG, weight 0.6, only 2 of 4 entries exported and nothing after the pickup \u2014 so whether he warned the rider of the deviation cannot be established, and the case should go to a human reviewer under POL-GEN-26. That is not accepted. Whether the rider was told is not a condition of row (d): row (d) applies to a non-traffic-justified reroute whether or not the rider was informed, and consent would not move the case into a no-refund row either. The impaired chat log therefore carries no fact this ruling needs, it does not cap confidence, and it does not force escalation. The rider's related points \u2014 that no exported message announces a deviation, and that the rider's 'ok 2 min' answers a pickup message rather than assenting to a Thomson Road route \u2014 are noted and consistent with that; they simply do not change the outcome.\n\nThe forum: the disputed value is 3.00 SGD, below POL-GEN-22's 10.00 SGD AI-final line, both profiles show fraud_flags 0 so the 0.95 band is not engaged, and the route-deviation confidence bar is 0.80 (POL-RD-25). POL-RD-25's 2 km limb is not in force because route_deviation.thresholds.ai_ruling_max_deviation_applied is false, and the deviation is under 2 km in any event. The deciding facts \u2014 the recorded distances, the traffic advisory and the per-km rate \u2014 are all carried by complete artifacts at weight 1.0, so confidence is 0.90, above the bar."
  },
